// A macOS program's image is known by the path the kernel passed in apple[0]
// ("executable_path=..."), and by the (device, inode) the file had when the program started
// (recorded first thing in main by __ablaRuntimeDarwinRecordImage; a program built by a
// compiler without that hook records at its first use). A path that no longer names that file (an
// install renamed another over it) does not resolve: the caller sees ENOENT, never another
// program's bytes. State words: +0 0 not recorded yet, 1 recorded, 2 unknown (no path or no
// stat); +8 device, +16 inode, +24 path address (a mapping), +32 path length.
