// affinity mask: every CPU hw.activecpu counts (sysctlbyname 274, an int) is in it, the lowest bits of `mask` set, as Linux
// writes it, in whole 8-byte words; the bytes written, or EINVAL (22) when `size` cannot hold them. Without it the call
// answered ENOSYS and every Mac's collector ran on one thread.
